    "result_text": "The full suite is green (there's a single runnable test class, `AcceptanceTest`; the others are support classes). BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), documenting it as the country code, a space, then national digits grouped in threes (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`).\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` plus a `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` default method that derives the display form. I put this in the mapper alongside the other pure read-only derivations (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`), so every read path (get/list/create) returns it consistently. The country-code split mirrors the `TelephoneNormalizer`'s recognised calling codes (`+61` \u2192 9 national digits, `+1` \u2192 10), with a safe fallback of a single leading digit for anything unrecognised, and returns the raw value untouched when it isn't in E.164 form.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is left exactly as-is (canonical E.164), so `$.telephone` stays `+61412345678` and `$.telephoneDisplay` renders `+61 412 345 678`, matching the acceptance test.",
